From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:39:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] device: renew an expiring token, and return errors instead of
 panicking.

ensure_device_credentials re-authenticated the device only when its STS token was missing, so a
service that ran past the token's expiry kept sending an expired one. It also panicked when
Microsoft could not be reached or the keychain refused. It now renews a token that expires within
five minutes, returns the device's STS token, and returns a DeviceError that tells keychain
refusals from Microsoft's. The CLI prints the error and fails.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: service-lifecycle
